# Binary assets committed directly to git (no LFS yet — see
# REPOSITORY_AUDIT.md §4). Mark them binary so they're never diffed/merged as text.
*.mp4 -diff -text
*.docx -diff -text

# scripts/context-budget.py measures CLAUDE.md by raw byte size (bytes // 4).
# On a checkout with core.autocrlf=true, CRLF adds ~1 byte per line (~970 for
# CLAUDE.md), which inflated the measurement over the 16,000-token budget and
# failed the gate on Windows checkouts while passing on Linux. Pin it to LF so
# the measurement is the same everywhere. A repo-wide `* text=auto eol=lf`
# normalization (matching .editorconfig) is the fuller fix — deferred because it
# rewrites line endings in every .js/.html file at once.
CLAUDE.md text eol=lf

# scripts/omega-registry.py measures every SKILL.md / agent .md and commits the
# result to OMEGA_SKILL_REGISTRY.md, which `--check` gates on. Pinning these to
# LF keeps a fresh checkout byte-identical across platforms. It is NOT what
# makes that gate deterministic: an attribute only controls what a checkout
# *writes*, and the self-hosted Windows runner reuses its working directory --
# with `eol=lf` in effect git reads an already-CRLF file back as LF, finds it
# clean against the index, and never rewrites it, so stale CRLF bytes persist
# and inflated the measurement by one byte per line. That is fixed in
# approx_tokens(), which normalises before counting; this pin is hygiene on top.
.claude/skills/**/*.md text eol=lf
.claude/agents/*.md text eol=lf
